You have left this choice open, and each option gives a different result:
- "how active each TF is in every sample": GIRAFFE gives each TF's activity in each sample, estimated apart from its own mRNA level.
- "the wiring diagram of which TF controls which gene": PANDA gives one weighted TF-to-gene regulatory network across all the samples given; OTTER gives one weighted TF-to-gene regulatory network across all samples, fitted so that it agrees with the PPI network and gene co-expression; LIONESS-PANDA gives one TF-gene network per sample, plus the aggregate network.

